       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the maximum standard dose.\n- **A second agent.** If 10 mg isn't enough, you could add an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-type diuretic. Combination therapy is generally preferred over going above 10 mg.\n- **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily, as written.** If you want this dose for a specific reason, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's intentional and above the labeled maximum.\n\nWhich would you like?"
